## Starting a session

Do not read a feature folder. Ask the hub for the intent you have:

```bash
node .agents/_tools/hub.mjs route <feature> --intent <resume|business|implementation|release|operations>
node .agents/_tools/hub.mjs status <feature>     # add --json for MR ids, branches, commits
```

`route` returns prose only; `status` is the only place delivery state lives. Run both when you are
picking work up. `plans/_REGISTRY.md` lists every feature (generated — never hand-edit it).
`.agents/README.md` has the full route table.

## Writing back

Each document answers ONE question. Write what you learned into the document that owns that
question — the map is `.agents/plans/_INSTRUCTION.md` §"Where to write". Never write into whichever
file you happened to have open, and never record the same fact twice.

After changing plans, tooling or skills, run `hub.mjs doctor`, `hub.mjs registry check`, and
`graph.mjs build && graph.mjs broken`.

## Context contract

- `.agents/` is agent-only. The operator does not read it and will ask you instead: explain outcome,
  impact, evidence, current state and next action in full, never a bare internal identifier.
- Never equate a merged change with a deployed or runtime-verified change. Lifecycle, merge,
  deployment and QC are four independent facts per environment; unproven evidence stays `unknown`.
- Project-specific configuration, scripts, and skills live in `.agents/_config/`,
  `.agents/scripts/`, and `.agents/skills/` — never in the shared frame.

